{{Quote|This is my city. These are my people. I will not abandon them.|Boba Fett|<ref name="Chapter 7">{{BOBF|Chapter 7: In the Name of Honor}}</ref>}}
'''Mos Espa''' was a [[spaceport]] settlement located on the [[desert]] [[Planet|world]] of [[Tatooine]]. The settlement included a number of commercial and workspace settings, as well as entertainment establishments such as the [[Mos Espa Grand Arena]]. During the [[Invasion of Naboo]], Mos Espa was also home to a number of [[Slavery|slaves]], including [[Anakin Skywalker]] and his [[Parent|mother]], [[Shmi Skywalker Lars|Shmi]].

==Description==
{{Quote|I hear Mos Espa is known for podracing and gambling. I do not care much for podracing, but I know the way around a casino like the back of my hand.|Diago Velaar|<ref name="Hunters">''[[Star Wars: Hunters]]''</ref>}}
One of the few [[Spaceport|port]] [[City|cities]] on the [[Outer Rim Territories|Outer Rim]] [[planet]] of [[Tatooine]],<ref name="Databank" /> the huge city of Mos Espa<ref name="World Building">{{InsiderCite|227|World Building (Star Wars Insider 227)}}</ref> was filled with dwellings, workplaces, and commercial operations of many kinds, along with entertainment venues, some of which were grandiose in size.<ref name="Databank" /> The [[crime lord]] [[Jabba Desilijic Tiure]] maintained a [[Jabba's casino|casino]] in Mos Espa.<ref name="Star Wars 38" /> The [[Mos Espa Grand Arena]], home to the [[Boonta Eve Classic]] [[Podracing|podrace]],<ref name="Episode I" /> could seat an audience numbering almost as many as the city's entire population. Because the [[Hutt]]s controlled Mos Espa and found the institution of [[slavery]] to be very useful, slaves were often traded within the city.<ref name="Databank" /> One such slave trader was the [[Toydarian]] [[Watto]], who owned a [[Watto's junkshop|parts store]]<ref name="Episode I" /> on the city outskirts.<ref name="World Building" /> The city center was located in a crater.<ref name="Chapter 3 audio description">{{BOBF|Chapter 3: The Streets of Mos Espa}} {{AD|Disney+}}</ref>

==History==
===Republic Era===
[[File:Mos_Espa_Grand_Arena.png|thumb|left|220px|The Boonta Eve Classic about to begin in the Mos Espa Grand Arena]]
Ten [[Standard year|years]] before the outbreak of the [[Clone Wars]] between the [[Galactic Republic]] and the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]], Mos Espa was visited by [[Queen]] [[Padmé Amidala Naberrie|Amidala]] of [[Naboo]], the [[Jedi Master]] [[Qui-Gon Jinn]], the [[Gungan]] [[Jar Jar Binks]], and the [[astromech droid]] [[R2-D2]], as their [[Starship|ship]] was in dire need of [[hyperdrive]] repairs. The party stopped by Watto's part store<ref name="Episode I" /> on the Mos Espa city outskirts,<ref name="World Building" /> where they met the young slave [[Anakin Skywalker]]. Unable to acquire the parts they needed, the group headed out, but due to a [[sandstorm]], Skywalker took them back to his house. There they met Anakin's mother [[Shmi Skywalker Lars|Shmi Skywalker]]. After a secret blood test, Jinn realized Anakin's [[midi-chlorian]] count was the highest of any [[Jedi]], and he thus began to believe Anakin was the [[Chosen One]], the one prophesied to destroy the [[Sith]] and bring balance to [[the Force]].<ref name="Episode I" />

Because of Anakin's access to the Force, Jinn attempted to free the boy from Watto by way of gambling on a podrace. The two agreed that, if Anakin won the race, Watto would hand over the parts needed for the hyperdrive and free Anakin. If Anakin were to lose, Jinn would have to give the entire ship over to Watto. Anakin went on to win the race, ensuring his freedom and acquiring the parts needed to fix the hyperdrive. He then left his mother to begin training as a member of the [[Jedi Order]].<ref name="Episode I" />

Just prior to the outbreak of the Clone Wars, Skywalker returned to Mos Espa in search of his mother, who had been the subject of numerous nightmares that had been keeping the Jedi from sleeping. Watto informed Skywalker that he had sold Shmi, and that her new owner [[Cliegg Lars]] had freed her and married her. Skywalker departed to find his mother after Watto showed him the location of the [[Lars homestead|Lars moisture farm]] on his map.<ref name="Episode II">{{Film|II}}</ref>

===Imperial and New Republic Eras===
[[File:MosEspaSpaceport-BoBFCh7.png|thumb|right|250px|Mos Espa spaceport around 9 ABY.]]
At one time, the businesswoman [[Laizhu Bedenn]] maintained a [[Laizhu Bedenn's diner|modest diner]] in Mos Espa that provided good food at reasonable prices. She became a role model and someone to go to for advice. However, after managing to keep up with the tribute payments Jabba the Hutt demanded of her, a sudden spike in requested payment born out of Jabba's greed proved to be too much. With Bedenn unable to pay, the angered Jabba forced her to work in the kitchens of his [[Boba Fett's Palace|palace]], where the only person who looked up to her was the young [[Waiter|waitress]] [[Valnir Nai]]. Shortly before Jabba's death, both managed to escape the palace on a stolen speeder.<ref name="Valnir and Laizhu" />

Around [[9 ABY]],<ref name="9 ABY">{{BoBFDate}}</ref> the [[Ithorian]] [[Mok Shaiz]] was mayor of Mos Espa and its surrounding plateaus. He sent his [[Mok Shaiz's majordomo|majordomo]] to receive tribute from the new [[Daimyo]] [[Boba Fett]], who had taken over [[Jabba's criminal empire]] to create [[Fett gotra|his own]]. When the former bounty hunter refused to pay this tribute, the Majordomo told the crime lord that he should expect a second delegation from the mayor sometime in the future.<ref name="Chapter 1" />

==Behind the scenes==
Mos Espa made its first [[canon]] appearance in the [[1999]] film [[Star Wars: Episode I The Phantom Menace|''Star Wars'': Episode I ''The Phantom Menace'']].<ref name="Episode I" /> It then appeared in the [[2002]] film [[Star Wars: Episode II Attack of the Clones|''Star Wars'': Episode II ''Attack of the Clones'']].<ref name="Episode II" /> The ''[[Star Wars Insider]]'' article "[[World Building (Star Wars Insider 227)|World Building]]" explained the seeming contradiction of how busy and huge Mos Espa is in ''[[Star Wars: The Book of Boba Fett]]'' compared to the prequel films, establishing that locations like Watto's junkshop and Slave Quarters Row were on the outskirts of the larger city. The article further hypothesizes that the Mos Espa Grand Arena and Watto's shop were part of the upper sprawl area.<ref name="World Building" />

